# Protocol context

**nudu Growth Protocol** is curated lending on Cardano: LatAm capital into revenue-based loans (RBF) to LatAm startups via **curator-managed tranched vaults** with a first-loss **junior** tranche.

## Phase 1 (MVP on-chain)

Build only:

- **Tranched vault** — USDCx deposits to senior or junior; native share tokens per tranche
- **Credit contract** — one UTxO per loan (terms, disbursement, repayments)
- **Waterfall** — senior rate first (pro rata among senior LPs), remainder to junior; losses hit junior first
- **KYC whitelist** — deposits only from whitelisted addresses
- **Revenue oracle** — one whitelisted attester; signed revenue attestations for repayments

Target network for deployment: **preprod** (when wiring deploy scripts). Do not scope mainnet-only integrations in phase-1 contracts.

## Out of scope for phase 1

Do not add validators, redeemers, or datums for:

- Idle liquidity (Liqwid, sUSDrf / RealFi Efficiency Layer)
- External curators or multi-vault factory beyond the single pilot vault
- Governance token or protocol tokenomics
- Public SDK or dashboard (off-chain only later)

Reference docs: [README.md](README.md), [docs/curated-lending-for-latam-startups.pdf](docs/curated-lending-for-latam-startups.pdf).

## Actors

| Actor | Role |
|-------|------|
| Senior depositors | LatAm LPs; paid first at lower rate |
| Curator | Selects borrowers, sets terms, funds junior (first loss); **single Ed25519 key** in MVP |
| Borrower | Startup; repays % of revenue per loan terms |
| Attester | Signs revenue attestations (one key in config for MVP) |

Investors deposit **directly into contracts** — the protocol must not introduce an off-chain custodial wallet for user funds.

## Fixed product rules

- **Denomination:** USDCx only for vault, loans, fees, and waterfall splits (integer base units).
- **No protocol token** in the next 12 months; fees are USDCx (protocol fee on interest, curator performance fee).
- **Scripts are immutable** after deploy: no upgrade proxy, no “replace script hash” redeemer in MVP.
- **Curator control** lives in **datum fields** and **whitelist mint policy**, not in redeploying validators.
